 ## Overview
 This module provides a PyTorch C++ extension containing CUDA kernels for ray sampling, alpha calculation, and weight accumulation in volume rendering [S1, unofficial]. It exposes low-level tensor operations for batched ray processing, enabling efficient GPU execution of point sampling, masking, and differentiable alpha blending [S1, unofficial].
-
 ## How it works
 ### Inputs and Outputs
 The interface consists of multiple CUDA kernels exposed via `pybind11` [S1, unofficial]. Each kernel accepts PyTorch tensors as inputs and returns PyTorch tensors or vectors of tensors as outputs [S1, unofficial]. All tensors are assumed to be on the same CUDA device [G].
-
 ### Data Structures
 The data structures are implicit in the tensor shapes defined by the kernel signatures [S1, unofficial].
