 ## Background
 This interface is part of the UnboundedNeRFPytorch implementation, an unofficial PyTorch port of NeRF-related methods for unbounded scenes [S1, unofficial]. It extends standard NeRF rendering pipelines by providing specialized kernels for ray-box intersection and sampling, which are crucial for handling large, unbounded volumes efficiently [S1, unofficial]. The code is based on the `render_utils.cpp` module from the original NeRF implementations, adapted for PyTorch's autograd system [S1, unofficial].
